    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0443" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/2–2845</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-28">February 28,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I desire that you, as Secretary of State, assume the responsibility for seeing
                    that the conclusions, exclusive of course of military matters, reached at the
                    Crimea Conference, be carried forward. In so doing you will, I know, wish to
                    confer with other officials of this Government on matters touching upon their
                    respective fields. I will expect you to report to me direct on the progress you
                    are making in carrying the Crimea decisions into effect in conjunction with our
                    Allies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ranklin</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
